@startuml sequence_export_experiment
!theme plain
title Experiment Export – Browse -> Backend -> Browser Download

actor User
participant "Browse Page\n(Streamlit)" as Browse
participant "FastAPI\n/app.py" as API
participant "db.py\n(SQLite WAL)" as DB
participant "export_import.py\n(zip builder)" as Export
participant "File System\n(results)" as FS
participant "Browser\n(download)" as Browser

== User selects runs / experiment ==
User -> Browse: select runs in table
Browse -> Browse: user opens "📦 Export / Import" sidebar
Browse -> Browse: choose artifact checkboxes\n(☐ frames, ☐ TensorBoard, ☐ trajectories)

== Individual run export ==
User -> Browse: click "⬇ Download selected runs"
Browse -> Browse: build_run_export_url(run_dirs, flags)
Browse -> Browser: st.link_button(url=<backend>/runs/export?...)
Browser -> API: GET /runs/export?run_dirs=...&include_frames=...
API -> Export: build_run_export_zip(run_dirs, flags)
Export -> FS: read manifest.json, metrics.csv, summary.json
opt include_frames
    Export -> FS: read frames/*.png
end
Export --> API: zip bytes (StreamingResponse)
API --> Browser: application/zip (streamed chunks)
Browser --> Browser: native download with progress bar

== Full experiment export ==
User -> Browse: click "Export experiment" (grouped view)
Browse -> Browse: build_experiment_export_url(exp_id, flags)
Browse -> Browser: st.link_button(url=<backend>/experiments/{id}/export?...)
Browser -> API: GET /experiments/{exp_id}/export?include_frames=...
API -> DB: get_experiment(exp_id)
DB --> API: experiment record (spec, status, run_dirs, ...)
API -> Export: create_experiment_export_zip_generator(...)
Export -> FS: read _spec.json, _result.json
Export -> FS: read each run_dir (manifest, metrics, optional artifacts)
Export -> Export: build zip in temp file
Export --> API: yield 1 MiB chunks
API --> Browser: StreamingResponse (chunked)
Browser --> Browser: native download with progress bar

@enduml
